==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|fr}} from {{etyl|VL.|fr}} {{m|la|*falcāre}} or {{m|la|*falciāre}} (compare Italian {{term|falciare|lang=it}}), from {{etyl|la|fr}} {{term|falx|falx, falcis|sickle, scythe|lang=la}} (compare {{term|faucille|lang=fr}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|fr}} {{m|ine-pro|*dhalk-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*dhalg-||a cutting tool}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-faucher.ogg|audio|lang=fr}}
* {{IPA|/foʃe/|lang=fr}}

===Verb===
{{fr-verb}}

# to {{l|en|mow}}, to {{l|en|reap}}
# to {{l|en|run over}}, to {{l|en|knock down}}

